  "id": "COMPOUND:21717 - PROTEIN:3966",
  "verbalization": "Ligustrone A is shown to have a target relationship with Receptor-type tyrosine-protein phosphatase beta through multiple pathways, with the most direct link emerging from the interaction between Ligustrone A and HCT-8, which is then targeted by Npc117493 and 6-Ethyl-4-hydroxy-5-methyl-3-[[2,4,6-trihydroxy-3-(3-methyl-2-butenyl)-5-(2-methyl-1-oxopropyl)phenyl]methyl]-2 h-pyran-2-one. These compounds are all implicated in targeting Receptor-type tyrosine-protein phosphatase beta, suggesting a shared mechanism of action. The evidence is supported by a consistent pattern of target relationships, with the core mechanism likely involving the inhibition of tyrosine-protein phosphatase activity. The presence of multiple overlapping targets and the involvement of a common intermediate compound (6-Ethyl-4-hydroxy-5-methyl-3-...) further strengthens the hypothesis that Ligustrone A exerts its effects through a pathway that modulates this receptor. The integration of these findings supports a mechanistic link between Ligustrone A and Receptor-type tyrosine-protein phosphatase beta, though further validation with in vitro or in vivo studies is warranted to confirm the biological relevance.",
